1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,640
For most of my adult life, I work with things you can measure, data, models, dashboards,

2
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:12,800
the clean grammar of proof.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:22,560
I am not the kind of person who cries at lines on a page, except I do.

4
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:29,680
Not in public, but sometimes a poem finds the exact nerve, no dataset ever mapped and

5
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:31,560
something releases.

6
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:36,160
I did not plan for that, I don't have a flame book for it, I have stopped pretending

7
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:43,320
the last two lives are separate, poetry is supposed to stay in its lane, literature

8
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:51,280
class, soft cover journals, the corner of life designated for feelings, you can't organize.

9
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:57,600
It doesn't stay there, it shows up in a line of code, you wrote at 2am that reads like

10
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,280
confession.

11
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:04,520
In the way your mother once described rain, in the grief that arrived when a number on

12
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:09,680
a screen told you something true, that you weren't ready for.

13
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:16,320
The lyric form is the one that admits what human experience refuses to sort.

14
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:21,400
That's not a romantic claim, that's just accurate.

15
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:28,880
Here is the thing about elegant code, programmers call it beautiful, they always have, there's

16
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:36,480
a reason for that, a specific moment, a commit message, a recursive function, a line of

17
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:43,280
output that felt like a volta, something real and particular.

18
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:49,760
Some weeks I built Ashboards, review model outputs, stare at analytics, other weeks I write

19
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:56,200
poems, nobody may ever read, for years I kept those as separate identities, then I noticed

20
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:02,920
the same thing drove both, the desire to understand what people actually feel beneath

21
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:06,000
what they say.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:18,360
One used numbers, the other used metaphor, tools different, curiosity identical.

23
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:25,440
The best scientific papers have rhythm, the best commit messages have grief in them sometimes,

24
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:31,640
poetry was already in the server room, it was never waiting for an invitation.

25
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:39,080
The toast burns, you scrape it over the sink, that smell, charred edges, still warm bread

26
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:46,400
underneath, you have done this a hundred times, but one morning a poem lives inside it,

27
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:55,400
not one you write, one you inhabit, briefly before the day takes over.

28
00:02:55,400 --> 00:03:02,480
poetry is not elevated experience, it's for its ordinary experience seen clearly for

29
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:10,920
one second, the gray of a commute counts, the brown of bad coffee counts, the particular

30
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:20,720
blue of a Tuesday afternoon, when nothing happens and you feel inexplic- the particular blue

31
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:31,480
of a Tuesday afternoon, when nothing happens and you feel inexplicable, the particular blue

32
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:42,280
of a Tuesday afternoon, when nothing happens and you feel inexplicably okay.

33
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:48,000
You don't have to write any of this down, notice it did not come from somewhere special,

34
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:55,080
notice it came from Tuesday, no one sits down to feel grief poetically, it arrives unannounced

35
00:03:55,080 --> 00:04:01,960
in the wrong font, but grief has always been poetry's country, not because poets romanticize

36
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:12,120
laws, the best ones don't, because grief insists on specificity.

37
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:17,440
If you don't miss a person, you miss how this said your name, the exact pitch of their

38
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:23,600
laugh at something stupid, there are losses I can summarize in a sentence, others I can

39
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:27,000
approach through poems.

40
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:36,720
Facts tell you, facts tell you what happened, poetry tells you what stayed behind after it

41
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:39,440
happened.

42
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:47,240
It's not a small mercy, it's the reason people reach for poems at funerals and not spreadsheets.

43
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:54,080
The Times Poetry has landed heart-ass on me, I wasn't looking for it, I was tired,

44
00:04:54,080 --> 00:05:02,400
half reading, distracted by something smaller, that's the trap in waiting for elevated moments.

45
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:08,000
Poetry comes sideways, in a lyric you have heard 40 times, that suddenly means something

46
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:14,080
different, and a sentence someone says to you that you'll carry for years without knowing

47
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:16,120
why.

48
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:22,440
It dips its fingers in every color, because it's patient, it waits in the ordinary and

49
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:30,400
the technical and the unbearable until you're open, just barely, and then it reaches you.

50
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:36,160
The door doesn't need to be wide, a crack is enough.

51
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:43,440
There is no lesson here, that's the point, poetry doesn't sharpen your frameworks, it doesn't

52
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:50,480
solve problems, it makes you a person who has stood inside a color, briefly, and recognized

53
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:57,080
it for what it was, and that's not a small thing, it's the whole thing.

54
00:05:57,080 --> 00:06:04,160
The poem finds you, your only job is to not keep the door entirely shut.

55
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:08,800
If a line has stayed with you, something that you read years ago that still lives in your

56
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:15,120
chest, I would love to hear it, find me on Instagram at mistakenly human, that's the

57
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:18,440
whole ask, one line that followed you home, bring it.

